/**

@page tutorials_exahype2_applications_exagrype_clusters Run ExaGRyPE on Clusters

Using ExaGRyPE on clusters is straightforward in principle, the correct configure command will allow
you run the code in parallel automatically. However, the module you need to load is usually different
in name as the convention is not unified. We kindly encourage users to contribute to this page by
sharing their setups if they have successfully run ExaGRyPE on their clusters.

# Compiling on COSMA

the suggest loading module and setup (before compiling the Peano kernel) when you use COSMA or DINE are

~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
module purge
module load intel_comp/2024.2.0
module load compiler-rt tbb compiler mpi 
export FLAVOUR_NOCONFLICT=1
module load python
export I_MPI_CXX=icpx
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

# Compiling on Hamilton

the suggest loading module when you use Hamilton are

~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
module purge
module load intel/2024.2
module load compiler-rt tbb compiler mpi 
module load python/3.10.8
export I_MPI_CXX=icpx
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

# SLURM script

The following script gives an exmaple for submitting ExaGRyPE job to the cluster via SLURM system.

~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
#!/bin/bash -l

#SBATCH -o %A.out
#SBATCH -e %A.err
#SBATCH -p bluefield1
#SBATCH -A durham
#SBATCH -t 24:00:00
#SBATCH --ntasks-per-node=1
#SBATCH --nodes=2
#SBATCH -J ExaGRyPE

echo "My SLURM_ARRAY_TASK_ID: " $SLURM_ARRAY_TASK_ID

module purge
module load intel_comp/2024.2.0
module load compiler-rt tbb compiler mpi 
export FLAVOUR_NOCONFLICT=1
module load python

export UCX_TLS=ud,sm,self

export OMP_NUM_THREADS=32

mpirun ./peano4_test
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~


*/

